From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:05:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09842/11362] [outer-loop] Un-retire exp6582: it was retired
 for its environment, half of it ours

Reverses the retirement in 613d227da1, which survived two of my own
corrections (aaf899eca4, 3f284b9eaa) before an independent audit refuted
the justification itself. All prior text is kept verbatim in both files.

BOTH BLOCKING PRECONDITIONS ARE ENVIRONMENTAL, not properties of the
experiment.

  verification_commands  required a green repo-wide test suite before a
                         model could load. Since demoted out of the
                         pre-launch gate (REQ-REPORT-6581-VERIFY-SCOPE).
  idle_supported_gpu     failed because the box was contended. The
                         contention was this outer loop's own seed sweep,
                         which has held GPU 1 continuously for 19+ hours.

An experiment retired because its environment was broken is wrongly
retired, and I supplied half the broken environment while writing the
retirement.

CLAUDE.md's Pre-Launch Preconditions Discipline says blocked_* verdicts
are honest non-terminal states that should not burn the doomed-rerun
ledger. Retiring on a repeated blocked_* verdict was the wrong
instrument, whatever the rerun count.

THE RED-SUITE CLAIM IN MY OWN MANIFEST TEXT IS NOT SOURCED FROM THESE
ARTIFACTS. Verified directly rather than taken from the audit: each
artifact carries eighteen exit_code 0 values and a single exit_code 124,
a TIMEOUT. The repo-wide suite is genuinely red, but that lives in
ops/known-issues.md from separate runs. These two runs timed out. They
did not observe 68-470 failures, and I wrote that they did.

The entry's own reopen condition -- a diagnosed cause plus a statement of
what changed -- is met. Diagnosis: verification_commands at
experiment_6581_qwen36_flagship_source_shard.py:1513. What changed: the
check is demoted and repaired.

Neither experiment is retired now. The entry is KEPT rather than deleted:
its scope_key and blocked_patterns still describe a real shape worth
matching if it recurs with a diagnosed cause, and three rounds of wrong
reasoning by one author is worth leaving legible.

Verified through the real code path, not by reading the file:
is_excluded returns False for 6581, 6582 and a control id. Activation
lint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
